  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p>The correct answer is: <b>If stacks were not created with the custom cookbooks feature enabled, you can resolve this by simply modifying the stack’s settings to include custom cookbooks.</b></p><p>This means that even if you forgot to enable custom cookbooks during the initial stack creation in AWS OpsWorks, you still have the ability to go to the stack’s settings and turn this feature on. Once enabled, you can then manage and assign your Chef recipes as needed.</p><p>Let’s consider why the other choices are incorrect:</p><ul><li><i>You can’t assign custom recipes once a stack exists; they must be configured during initial stack setup.</i> – This isn’t accurate. AWS OpsWorks allows you to update stack settings to enable the use of custom cookbooks, so you are not locked out if you missed the setting at creation.</li><li><i>After layers are added to a stack, custom recipes become unassignable; they should only be designated at the time of layer creation.</i> – This is incorrect because custom recipes can be assigned to layers at any time, provided that custom cookbooks have been defined in the stack.</li><li><i>If your stack's layers were set up without enabling custom cookbooks, you just need to adjust the individual layer settings to add custom recipes.</i> – This option is misleading. While you can assign custom recipes at the layer level, the crucial prerequisite is that the stack itself must first have custom cookbooks enabled; changing layer settings alone won’t help if the stack setting is missing.</li></ul><p><strong>Tip:</strong> In AWS OpsWorks, always ensure the stack has custom cookbooks enabled before attempting to add or assign custom recipes to your stacks or layers.</p>",
  "query": "<p>Your company has set up various infrastructure resources in AWS, which you are now responsible for managing. You want to incorporate your organization’s Chef recipes into the existing AWS OpsWorks stacks. However, when attempting to add these recipes, you notice there isn’t an available option to do so in the recipes section. What is the most likely explanation for this situation?</p>",
